{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "A Night at the Planetarium"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Getting Tickets"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand detailed descriptions of real or imaginary events and experiences in present, past or future, in spoken interactions or written texts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts"}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex texts on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Might</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Could</span>, <span class=\"italic\">May</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Can't</span> to Speculate about the Present"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the modal verbs <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span>, <span class=\"italic\">could</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may</span> and <span class=\"italic\">can't</span> to speculate or make guesses about something in the present. The modal you choose depends on the level of probability you want to express."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The grammar structure:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Level of Certainty\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ base form of         the verb        <br>(verb without \u201cto\u201d)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"almost certain\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"must\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ base form of         the verb        <br>(verb without \u201cto\u201d)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"it's possible\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"might<br>could<br>may\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ base form of         the verb        <br>(verb without \u201cto\u201d)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"it's very unlikely\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ base form of         the verb        <br>(verb without \u201cto\u201d)\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">must</span></span> for logical conclusions. There is a strong degree of certainty about the present situation and it's almost like you're making the \u201cbest guess\u201d about something that's happening in the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">may, might</span></span> and <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">could</span></span> to speculate about things in the present when there are other possibilities. These modals all have the same meaning."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">can't</span></span> when the situation is impossible."}, {"type": "example", "content": "This movie <span class=\"strong\">must</span> be very popular."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I believe it <span class=\"strong\">might</span> even surpass Avatar as the highest grossing film of all time."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I <span class=\"strong\">could</span> try using my credit card."}, {"type": "example", "content": "My credit card  <span class=\"strong\">may</span> be maxed out."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> wait util next time. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Will</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Won't</span> in the <span class=\"italic\">If</span>-clause to Express Polite Request or Refusal"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can ask someone to do something or refuse to do something politely by using <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">will</span></span> or <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">won't</span></span> in the <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"underline\">if</span>-clause</span>. <br>Using <span class=\"italic\">will</span> in the <span class=\"italic\">if</span>-clause for these reasons is different from expressing future possibility. <br>Remember, an <span class=\"italic\">if</span>-clause is a dependent clause and cannot stand alone. <br>It must be added to a dependent clause to make a complete sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the following structures to make polite requests, and show insistence and refusal."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">if + will</span></span>\u2192 polite request (this is similar to saying \u201cif you wouldn't mind\u201d)<br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If you'll just have a seat</span>, the doctor will see you shortly</span>. <br>(If you wouldn't mind having a seat, the doctor will see you shortly.)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">if + will</span></span>\u2192 insisting that someone do something (this is similar to saying \u201cif you insist on\u201d)<br> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If you will arrive at my house twenty minutes early</span>, you must expect to wait for me to finish getting dressed.</span><br> (If you insist on arriving at my house twenty minutes early, you must expect to wait for me to finish getting dressed.)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">if + won't</span></span>\u2192 polite refusal (this is similar to saying \u201cif you refuse to\u201d)<br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> If you won't come to the party with me</span>, we can stay home and watch movies instead</span>. <br>(If you refuse to come to the party with me, we can stay home and watch movies instead.)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">Pronunciation Note</span>: When speaking and reading aloud, remember to stress the word <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">won't</span></span> a little more."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">If</span> you <span class=\"strong\">won't</span> do it, I<span class=\"strong\">'ll</span> take it upon myself to do it. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">If</span> you<span class=\"strong\">'ll</span> do it, I<span class=\"strong\">'ll</span> be forever grateful."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "proposition"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "proposal"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Listen, I've got a proposition for you."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le01ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about leisure."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to surpass"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to go beyond"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I believe it might even surpass \u201c Avatar\u201d as the highest grossing film of all time."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le01ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to flock"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to come in large numbers"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:   People continue to flock to this movie even though it's two years old. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le01ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "maxed out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "at the limit"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:My credit card may be maxed out and I only have enough cash for my ticket and some popcorn. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le01ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hype"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "discussion that makes something seem more exciting than it actually is"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I really hope this movie is worth all this hype!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le01ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to decline"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to refuse"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I tried to use my card before and it was declined."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le01ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le01ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online or to your local library and look for information about the first movie you watched at a theater."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Find out as much as you can about it: date of release, premier week, how it did at the box office."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Reflect on when you watched it and how that experience was."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Tell your partner about the information you found and also describe the time you watched it"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Express your opinion about your partner's movie."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read information about a movie."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about my experience of going to the theater."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about other's people preferences."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le01ob03re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le01ob03re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le01ob03re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Wow! Look at the crazy lineup. I haven't seen the theater this crowded since <span class=\"italic\">Titanic</span>. This movie must be very popular.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: It is. I have been waiting for it for almost two years. I believe it might even surpass <span class=\"italic\">Avatar</span> as the highest grossing film of all time.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Well, if people continue to flock to this movie at this rate, I am sure this movie will beat <span class=\"italic\">Avatar</span> by next weekend.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le01ob03re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I agree with you.  Oh no!\n<br><span class=\"strong\">John</span>: What's wrong?\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I can't find my wallet. I must have left it on the coffee table at home.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">John</span>: That's not good.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Listen, I've got a proposition for you. If you cover my movie and popcorn, I'll get you dinner tomorrow.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">John</span>: I don't know about that Peter. My credit card may be maxed out and I only have enough cash for my ticket and some popcorn.", "id": 2, "time": "24500", "image": "engenn10le01ob03re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Let's try using your credit card. If it isn't too much to ask, there's nothing else we can do.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">John</span>: I don't think it will work Peter.  I tried it before and it was declined.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: It has to work John! I have been waiting to watch this movie for years. If you won't do it, I'll take it upon myself to do it.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Relax Peter! It's not a big deal. If it's okay with you, there's always next time.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I can't wait until next time. Please try! If you'll do it, I'll be forever grateful.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Okay, okay Peter calm down. I really hope this movie is worth all the hype!", "id": 3, "time": "48500", "image": "engenn10le01ob03re2img04.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about science and leisure time."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "  I can discuss going out and socializing.  "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can explain my opinion, and make and refuse polite requests using <span class=\"italic\">if</span>. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Have you ever wanted to go to movie premieres? Which movies? Why?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Have you ever been to a movie premiere? Was it crowded?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "What's the highest grossing film of all time?"}], "template_override": 1}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "id": 1}]}], "stimuli_ids": [1], "id": 1, "type": "STI", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "John and Peter are waiting in line."}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2